    {
      "name": "problem_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly answers the query by categorizing recurring incident types, giving a strong axis to group and count problems. Values are well-grounded in short_description (VPN, WiFi, Database, Internet all match). One minor concern: 'Email system not working' mapped to 'Email Client' is a slightly arbitrary specific where the text is ambiguous between client/server, but overall categorization is sound."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_connectivity_issue",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.45,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A binary flag that is largely derivable from problem_type, making it partly redundant; it adds a coarse grouping axis but limited independent leverage. Groundedness is undermined by inconsistency: 'Cannot connect to database' (Database Access) is labeled false while VPN/WiFi/Internet are true, so the boundary is not consistently applied to what the text describes as connectivity."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_days",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.05,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Entirely NULL (500/500), so it provides no analytical leverage and is near-constant. It is also not relevant to the 'types of problems' query. Not hallucinated since it defaults to null rather than inventing values, but the empty column offers nothing."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
  "source_groundedness": 0.72,
  "rationale": "problem_type is a strong, directly-on-target column that meaningfully answers the recurring-problem-types query with well-grounded values. is_connectivity_issue is largely redundant with problem_type and applies its boundary inconsistently (database 'cannot connect' marked false). resolution_days is fully NULL, useless for this query, though not hallucinated. Overall the set is anchored by one excellent column with two weak additions; grounding is generally sound with minor inconsistency and no fabricated facts."
}

